&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in customer support strategy, CX operations or contact centre consulting/leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience designing and executing site strategy at scale (multi-site, multi-brand, international).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep workforce management expertise: forecasting, capacity planning, scheduling, real-time management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or sponsoring automation programmes, contact reduction, chatbot, AI agent-assist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of delivering headcount efficiencies without degrading quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modelling capability, built business cases independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working inside or alongside a fast-growth tech company or marketplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in food delivery, logistics or three-sided marketplace support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior exposure to DoorDash, Wolt or comparable platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background delivering inside complex integrations or M&amp;amp;A contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with WFM platforms (e.g. Verint, AWS Connect, Assembled, Calibrio) and CX tooling (e.g. Zendesk, Intercom).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ways of Working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The role requires deep, ongoing immersion in internal data, systems and teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All recommendations must arrive decision-ready.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The role operates with a high degree of autonomy, with regular visibility to leadership through written updates and reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalation discipline: flag blockers fast. Never sit on a problem for more than 48 hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectual honesty is non-negotiable.&lt;/li&gt;
